JS wave function:
```
const WAVES = [
 {dir:[1,0.25], amp:0.55, len:24, phase:0.0},
 ...
];
function waveInfo(x,z,t){
 let h=0,dx=0,dz=0;
 for w:
  const k=2π/w.len, omega=Math.sqrt(9.81*k)*0.55;
  const dl=Math.hypot(dirx,dirz); dirx/=dl...
  const ph=k*(dirx*x+dirz*z)-omega*t+w.phase;
  h += w.amp*Math.sin(ph);
  dx += w.amp*k*dirx*Math.cos(ph);
  dz += w.amp*k*dirz*Math.cos(ph);
 return {h, dx, dz};
}
```
Total amp = sum ~0.55+0.32+0.18+0.1+0.07 = 1.22. Good.

